=== SURVEY ===

1) Existing climate baseline (the AI-off canonical surface):
   - /climate-control route in web/src/App.tsx maps to
     features/vehicle-systems/pages/ClimateControlPage.tsx (the
     existing deterministic page).
   - Page contents (SURVEYED, NOT modified):
       * HVAC Status Banner (ClimateBanner)
       * Status grid: inside temp / outside temp / driver setting
         / climate on/off
       * Climate efficiency panel
       * Climate history table
       * Seat heater controls
       * Defrost / preconditioning toggles
       * Manual departure-time heuristic (deterministic ETA)
   - The page reads:
       useClimateLatest(activeIdNum)  ⇒  latest snapshot
       useClimateHistory(activeIdNum) ⇒  ChartContainer trends
       useClimatePreferences()        ⇒  user-pref defaults
   - Temperatures are SI-canonical Celsius on the API side
     (Phase-48): JSON shapes use `inside_temp_c`, `outside_temp_c`,
     `driver_temp_setting_c`.

2) Existing /climate route — DOES NOT EXIST. The slice prompt's
   "Frontend routes: /climate" line is the contract; the closest
   pre-existing surface is /climate-control. Decision: add an alias
   /climate ⇒ ClimateControl to App.tsx so the registry's published
   Frontend route is reachable, AND keep /climate-control unchanged
   (no breaking change for bookmarks).

3) Backend /api/v1/ai/climate/schedule/draft — DOES NOT EXIST. No
   conflict with the new route.

4) Tool registry (internal/ai/tools): no draft_climate_schedule or
   validate_climate_schedule tool exists. New file
   tools/preheat_precool_recommender.go owns both.

5) Strategy registry (internal/ai/features/registry.go): no
   "preheat-precool-recommender" entry exists. New entry needed.

6) Redaction policies (internal/ai/redact/policies.go): no policy
   for this feature. Decision: PolicyDigest equivalent — allow
   ClassVehicleName ONLY (so the LLM can address the user's
   vehicle by display name). All other PII classes (places,
   coordinates, addresses) stay tagged. The recommender is purely
   schedule-arithmetic — it does not need any other class.

7) Predecessor templates surveyed:
   - 0026 smart-charge-schedule-suggestion: same propose-only
     contract (draft_charge_schedule + validate_charge_schedule);
